messages.consumerWebCommon.accountModal.stampCard:
Defined terms have the same meaning as in the General Terms and Conditions Customers. {br}{br}
General Terms and Conditions Consumers: the most recent version of the general terms and conditions for consumers of {siteName}.{br}{br}
Participating Restaurant: a Restaurant that participates in the StampCards Programme and awards Stamps to Customers.{br}{br}
Stamp: Restaurant-specific Stamp that is awarded for every Order placed with a Participating Restaurant.{br}{br}
StampCard: Restaurant-specific overview of collected Stamps by a Customer, received by email, which is full and complete after having collected five Stamps.
{br}{br}
StampCards Programme: award programme that allows Customers to collect Stamps from Participating Restaurants on a StampCards which is full and complete after having collected five Stamps from the same Participating Restaurant and then results in a StampCards Voucher, which is redeemable with an Order with that Participating Restaurant. {br}{br}
StampCards Voucher: Restaurant-specific Voucher derived from a full StampCard, with a value of {amount}% of the total Order amount of the five Orders for which the Stamps were collected.{br}{br}
Terms and Conditions StampCards Customers: these terms and conditions in respect of the StampCards Programme of {siteName}, as amended from time to time.

1. To subscribe to the StampCards Programme, a Customer is required to sign up for the newsletter with a valid email address.{br}{br}
2. By signing up for the newsletter, a Customer agrees that these Terms and Conditions StampCards Customers will apply to the relationship between {siteName} and the Customer and will also apply to the relationship between the Customer and one or more Participating Restaurants, which will be established as a consequence of the Customer’s subscription to the StampCards Programme.{br}{br}
3. A Restaurant decides at its sole discretion whether or not to participate in the StampCards Programme.{br}{br}
4. The General Terms and Conditions Customers continue to apply to the relationship between {siteName} and the Customer, unless they explicitly differ from these Terms and Conditions StampCards Restaurants. In that situation the latter will prevail.{br}{br}
5. {siteName} may refuse at its sole discretion the subscription of a Customer in the StampCards Programme.

6. Stamps and StampCards Vouchers have no monetary or cash value and cannot be converted into any currency.{br}{br}
7. Stamps are awarded to the Customer exclusively by a Participating Restaurant.
8. {siteName} is the sole technical provider of the StampCards Programme, publishing the StampCards Programme on its Platform.{br}{br}
9. Customers with a valid email address will automatically receive 1 Stamp for every Order placed with a Participating Restaurant.{br}{br}
10. After placing an Order with a Participating Restaurant, a Customer that is signed up for the newsletter will automatically receive an email within 48 hours, showing the up-to-date overview of StampCards. A maximum of seven StampCards from Participating Restaurants will be displayed, sorted by the number of Stamps.{br}{br}
11. A StampCards is full and complete after five Stamps are collected from the same Participating Restaurant. A StampCards Voucher will be emailed to the Customer within 48 hours after the StampCards was completed.{br}{br}
12. Stamps expire 12 months from the date such Stamps have been awarded to the Customer.{br}{br}
13. Stamps are not transferable between Participating Restaurants, Customers, email addresses, StampCards or otherwise. {br}{br}
14. Customers are required to report any inaccuracies in their collected Stamps to {siteName}’s customer service within one month of discovering such inaccuracies.{br}{br}
15. {siteName} has the right:{br}{br}• to correct any unjustly awarded Stamps; or {br}{br}• to correct Stamps that were awarded while the Order and/ or {br}{br} • payment thereof was cancelled; and {br}{br} • to annul any StampCards Vouchers that are redeemed with such Stamps.

16. A StampCards Voucher:{br}{br} • can only be redeemed with an Order with the Participating Restaurant from which the Stamps were received;{br}{br} • can only be redeemed in combination with an online payment; and{br}{br} • cannot be combined with other vouchers of any kind.{br}{br} • is valid on any order via Thuisbezorgd.nl, excluding restricted products such as alcohol, tobacco and any other age-restricted items (see checkout page for details of any items voucher will not apply to).{br}{br}
17. The value of a StampCards Voucher equals 10% of the total Order amount of the five Orders for which the Stamps were collected.{br}{br}
18. The StampCards Voucher does not have to be redeemed with a single Order, but can be applied to as many Orders as necessary until the complete value of the StampCards Voucher is used.{br}{br}
19. The StampCards Voucher is redeemable for up to 90 days after the StampCards Voucher was issued. {br}{br}
20. After expiration of the StampCards Voucher, the Stamps that were used to complete that StampCards Voucher will not be returned to the Customer. {br}{br}

21. {siteName} can alter these Terms and Conditions StampCard Customers and any aspect of the StampCard Programme, including redemption procedures and rewards in any respect, all without prior notice. For example, this includes, but is not limited to: adding, deleting, or changing time limits for collection or redemption or use of Stamps or StampCard Vouchers. {siteName} will publish the amended Terms and Conditions StampCard Customers on the Platform.{br}{br}
21. A Customer’s continued participation in the StampCard programme constitutes his/ her acceptance of any changes to these Terms and Conditions StampCard Customers.{br}{br}
22. A Customer can choose to leave the StampCard Programme at any time. {br}{br} 23. Customers leave the StampCard Programme by unsubscribing from the newsletter. By leaving the StampCard Programme, a Customer terminates the relationship with {siteName} with respect to the StampCard Programme and forfeits the right to any Stamps accrued.{br}{br}
24. {siteName} reserves the right to cancel the StampCard Programme at any time without prior notice. In the case of cancellation of the StampCard Programme, Customers can no longer collect Stamps. However, StampCard Vouchers will remain valid until their expiration date.  {br}{br}
25. A Participating Restaurant is free to terminate its participation in the 
StampCard Programme at any time without notice to Customers. In the case of termination by a Participating Restaurant, a Customer can no longer collect Stamps from that Restaurant. However, StampCard Vouchers from that Restaurant remain valid until their expiration date.  {br}{br}
26. {siteName} reserves the right to withhold or suspend a Customer from collecting Stamps in the case of a (suspected) violation of the General Terms and Conditions Consumers or these Terms and Conditions StampCard Customers.

Website Terms and Conditions: the most recent version of the general terms and conditions for consumers of {siteName}.{br}{br}
Participating Restaurant: a Restaurant that participates in the StampCard Programme and awards Stamps to customers.{br}{br}
Stamp: Restaurant-specific Stamp that is awarded for every online paidOrder placed by a logged in {siteName} Customer (guest checkout users excluded) with a Participating Restaurant.{br}{br}
StampCard: Restaurant-specific overview of collected Stamps by a customer, received by email, which is full and complete after having collected five Stamps.{br}{br}
StampCard Programme: award programme that allows you to collect Stamps from Participating Restaurants on a StampCard which is full and complete after having collected five Stamps from the same Participating Restaurant and then results in a StampCard Discount, which is redeemable with an Order with that Participating Restaurant.{br}{br}
StampCard Discount: Restaurant-specific discount derived from a full StampCard, with a value of {amount}% of the total food and / or drink value of the five Orders for which the Stamps were collected.{br}{br}
StampCard Terms and Conditions: these terms and conditions in respect to the StampCard Programme of {siteName}, as amended from time to time.

1. A StampCard Discount is automatically applied at the basket for an Order placed by you with a Participating Restaurant if the Order value is equal to or greater than the StampCard Discount value.{br}{br}
2. By placing an Order with a Participating Restaurant, you agree that these StampCard Terms and Conditions will apply to the relationship between you and {siteName} and will also apply to the relationship between you and one or more Participating Restaurants, which will be established as a consequence of placing an Order with a Participating Restaurant.{br}{br}
3. A Restaurant decides at its sole discretion whether or not to participate in the StampCard Programme and not all Restaurants on the Website are participating.{br}{br}
4. The Website Terms and Conditions continue to apply to the relationship between you and {siteName}, unless they explicitly differ from these StampCard Terms and Conditions. In that situation these terms will prevail.

5. Stamps and StampCard Discounts have no monetary or cash value and cannot be converted into cash.{br}{br}
6. Stamps are awarded to you exclusively by a Participating Restaurant.{br}{br}
7. {siteName} is the sole technical provider of the StampCard Programme, publishing the StampCard Programme on its Website.{br}{br}
8. You will automatically receive 1 Stamp for every online paid Order you place with a Participating Restaurant (guest checkout users are excluded).{br}{br}
9. After placing an Order with a Participating Restaurant, you will automatically receive an email within 48 hours, showing an up-to-date overview of StampCards. You will also be able to view your current Stamps in your account.{br}{br}
10. A StampCard is full and complete after five Stamps are collected from the same Participating Restaurant.{br}{br}
11.Stamps expire 12 months from the date that the Stamps have been awarded to you.{br}{br}
12. Stamps are not transferable between Participating Restaurants, customers, email addresses, StampCards or otherwise.{br}{br}
13. You are required to report any inaccuracies in collected Stamps to {siteName}’s customer service within one month of discovering such inaccuracies.{br}{br}
14. {siteName} has the right:{br}{br}
 a. to correct any unjustly or incorrectly awarded Stamps; or{br}{br}
 b. to correct Stamps that were awarded while the Order and/ or payment thereof was cancelled; and{br}{br}
 c. to annul any StampCard Discounts that are redeemed with such Stamps.

15. A StampCard Discount:{br}{br}
 a. can only be redeemed with an Order with the Participating Restaurant from which the Stamps were received;{br}{br}
 b. can only be redeemed in combination with an online payment;{br}{br}
 c. can be redeemed with other offers or vouchers provided that a voucher is not greater than the payment total following the application of the StampCard Discount;{br}{br}
 d. can only be redeemed for Orders that have a value which is equal to or greater than the StampCard Discount;{br}{br}
 e. may be carried over to your next Order until your StampCard Discount is capable of being redeemed as per clause 15(d).{br}{br}
16. The value of a StampCard Discount equals {amount}% of the total Order value that you paid (excluding any other offers or vouchers applied to the Order) for the five Orders for which the Stamps were collected.{br}{br}
17. The StampCard Discount must be redeemed with a single Order.{br}{br}
18. The StampCard Discount is issued within 24 hours of every 5th Order.{br}{br}
19. The StampCard Discount is redeemable for up to 90 days after the StampCard Discount was issued.{br}{br}
20. After expiration of the StampCard Discount, the Stamps that were used to complete that StampCard Discount will not be returned to you.

21. {siteName} can alter these StampCard Terms and Conditions and any aspect of the StampCard Programme, including redemption procedures and rewards in any respect, all without prior notice. For example, this includes, but is not limited to: adding, deleting, or changing time limits for collection or redemption or use of Stamps or StampCard Discounts. {siteName} will publish the amended StampCard Terms and Conditions on the Website.{br}{br}
22. Your continued participation in the StampCard programme after any alteration constitutes your acceptance of any changes to these StampCard Terms and Conditions.{br}{br}
23. {siteName} reserves the right to cancel the StampCard Programme at any time without prior notice. In the case of cancellation of the StampCard Programme, you can no longer collect Stamps. However, StampCard Discounts will remain valid until their expiration date.{br}{br}
24. A Participating Restaurant is free to terminate its participation in the StampCard Programme at any time without notice to you. In the case of termination by a Participating Restaurant, you can no longer collect Stamps from that Restaurant. However, StampCard Discounts from that Restaurant remain valid until their expiration date.{br}{br}
25. A Participating Restaurant may leave the Website. In the case of a Participating Restaurant no longer being on the Website, you can no longer collect Stamps from that Restaurant and your StampCard Discounts from that Restaurant will expire.{br}{br}
26. {siteName} reserves the right to withhold or suspend you from collecting Stamps in the case of a (suspected) violation of the Website Terms and Conditions or these StampCard Terms and Conditions.

